From aa447a7929190ca97edee802c6e7ebe9685bbda9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bishwanath Bastola <bishwa.bastola123@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 03:13:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] nakshatra worker_daemon: accept mode "solo" for a
 whole-model worker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Companion to the nakshatra repo's worker.py fix (same day): NKS_SMART_PLACEMENT
started producing route-whole chains for the first time today (after fixing
two identity bugs that had kept it dead since 2026-07-14), and placement.py's
route-whole planner emits mode="solo" for the single worker holding the whole
model. This daemon rejected it outright: "[daemon] bad mode 'solo' (expected
first|middle|last)" — exit 1 before ever loading the model or opening a port.

mode_last is the only one of the three parsed mode flags actually read
anywhere past the validation block (mode_first is checked once and never
again; has_token_embd/has_lm_head a few lines down are hardcoded true
regardless of mode, per their own comment — "client validates via cluster
yaml"). So solo only needs to also satisfy mode_last (drives the final-logits
output path) — set both mode_last and mode_first true for "solo" for
correctness/future-proofing even though only the former currently matters.
Purely additive: existing first/middle/last behavior is untouched.

Rebuilt llama-nakshatra-worker + llama-nakshatra-worker-fabric (same source).
Verified standalone before touching the live binary: loads the real
32-layer whole-model slice, prints "[daemon] ready", clean shutdown. Previous
binary backed up as llama-nakshatra-worker.pre-solo-mode.bak.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019iS9L5sCYHFtg16AbMyFem
---
 examples/nakshatra-spike/worker_daemon.cpp | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/examples/nakshatra-spike/worker_daemon.cpp b/examples/nakshatra-spike/worker_daemon.cpp
index 69874dcb..2c7eac89 100644
--- a/examples/nakshatra-spike/worker_daemon.cpp
+++ b/examples/nakshatra-spike/worker_daemon.cpp
@@ -297,11 +297,19 @@ int main(int argc, char ** argv) {
     }
     std::string sub_gguf = argv[1];
     std::string mode_str = argv[2];
-    bool mode_last  = (mode_str == "last");
-    bool mode_first = (mode_str == "first");
+    // 2026-09-12 (placement lane): "solo" — a whole-model worker holding EVERY layer, emitted by
+    // placement.py's route-whole planner (assignment_from_plan: mode="solo" when n==1). Runs the
+    // SAME final-logits path as "last" (mode_last is the only one of these three flags actually
+    // read anywhere below this block — mode_first is checked here and never again; has_token_embd
+    // /has_lm_head above are hardcoded true regardless of mode). Never accepted before today:
+    // NKS_SMART_PLACEMENT never produced a route-whole chain end to end until 2026-09-12, so this
+    // value was never exercised — first symptom was worker.py's OWN argparse (choices=[...])
+    // rejecting it before the daemon was ever reached; fixed there too, same day.
+    bool mode_last  = (mode_str == "last" || mode_str == "solo");
+    bool mode_first = (mode_str == "first" || mode_str == "solo");
     bool mode_mid   = (mode_str == "middle");
     if (!mode_last && !mode_first && !mode_mid) {
-        fprintf(stderr, "[daemon] bad mode '%s' (expected first|middle|last)\n", mode_str.c_str());
+        fprintf(stderr, "[daemon] bad mode '%s' (expected first|middle|last|solo)\n", mode_str.c_str());
         return 1;
     }
     int n_ctx        = argc > 3 ? atoi(argv[3]) : 256;
